Caveat: Impulsive's forward-filled label (burn instant -> end of window) makes its 'any overlap' recall/precision structurally easier to satisfy than Chemical/Electric's bounded bursts -- not directly comparable across classes. Also note 'any overlap' recall alone does not penalize flicker (a correctly-recalled true event can still contain stray wrong-class guesses); it's a spurious class's own precision that catches that.
